{"title":"Sentences to ponder","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/957675941/0/marginalrevolution~Sentences-to-ponder.html","date":1780471494000,"content":"<blockquote><p>In 2019, there were about 150,000 people working in autism therapy. Six years later, there were 654,000—more than the number of people who work in mining and logging, or telecommunications, or at the US Postal Service.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>That is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/DKThomp/status/2061799633425215525\" target=\"_blank\">from Derek Thompson</a>.  And here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/23/health/autism-therapy-clinics.html\" target=\"_blank\">the seven-minute nap story from the NYT:</a></p>\r\n<blockquote><p>At Compleat Kidz, a fast-growing chain of autism clinics based in North Carolina, the policy is firm: Naps cannot be longer than seven minutes before children are awakened to resume therapy. The company says this is necessary to prevent fraud since clinics can be paid only when children are awake and getting services. But it also allows the clinic to bill insurers or Medicaid for more hours.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>I do not even need to say “model this.”</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/sentences-to-ponder-139.html\">Sentences to ponder</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/957675941/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/957675941/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/957675941/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://asse